1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:06,649
This is Coach Connect, the new way clients register with the Kentucky SBDC and book

2
00:00:06,699 --> 00:00:10,616
their first coaching appointment, all in one visit.

3
00:00:10,666 --> 00:00:15,346
Let’s walk through it as a client, and see what happens behind the scenes.

4
00:00:15,946 --> 00:00:21,248
There are four steps: your details, your business, review and consent, and your

5
00:00:21,298 --> 00:00:23,180
appointment.

6
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:29,087
Our sample client is Maya Brooks, who runs a catering business in Louisville.

7
00:00:29,137 --> 00:00:31,725
Step one is her contact information.

8
00:00:31,775 --> 00:00:35,801
Clients who aren’t in business yet just use their home address.

9
00:00:35,851 --> 00:00:38,042
Not ready for one-on-one coaching?

10
00:00:38,092 --> 00:00:42,110
The banner up top points to the no-cost training calendar.

11
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:47,092
The ZIP code does the routing. The moment it’s typed, the form shows the center that

12
00:00:47,142 --> 00:00:49,930
serves her: Louisville.

13
00:00:50,030 --> 00:00:54,682
ZIPs outside our map go to the Eastern Kentucky intake team, so nobody hits a dead

14
00:00:54,732 --> 00:00:56,103
end.

15
00:00:56,303 --> 00:01:01,118
When she clicks Continue, her contact details are saved right away, even if she never

16
00:01:01,168 --> 00:01:02,840
finishes.

17
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:07,034
Step two asks where she is in her business journey:

18
00:01:07,084 --> 00:01:10,459
starting a business, or already in business.

19
00:01:10,509 --> 00:01:15,846
Already in business adds a few fields, and the form requires at least one full-time

20
00:01:15,896 --> 00:01:18,393
or part-time employee.

21
00:01:19,093 --> 00:01:22,240
Then, in her own words, how we can help.

22
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:29,629
Demographic questions come last. Each offers Prefer not to say, except Sex, which is

23
00:01:29,679 --> 00:01:34,243
Male or Female. None of it affects the coaching match.

24
00:01:35,143 --> 00:01:40,519
Step three puts every answer on one screen, with a link back to edit.

25
00:01:40,819 --> 00:01:46,202
Two boxes are required: the client agreement, and a certification that she’s eligible

26
00:01:46,252 --> 00:01:49,303
for taxpayer-funded services.

27
00:01:49,353 --> 00:01:52,310
Her signature has to match the name she entered.

28
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:55,658
The SBA mailing permission is optional.

29
00:01:55,758 --> 00:02:00,809
Register and choose appointment records her registration in Neoserra.

30
00:02:01,809 --> 00:02:04,963
Now she picks a coach from the center that serves her.

31
00:02:05,013 --> 00:02:08,807
Louisville shows each coach’s photo and specialties.

32
00:02:08,857 --> 00:02:13,764
Maya’s planning a storefront, so Claire Bridges, who lists restaurant and catering

33
00:02:13,814 --> 00:02:17,391
operations, is a natural fit.

34
00:02:17,691 --> 00:02:22,691
Her choice is saved, and Claire’s Calendly opens right in the page, with Maya’s name

35
00:02:22,741 --> 00:02:24,878
and email filled in.

36
00:02:25,378 --> 00:02:28,184
She picks a time, and she’s on the calendar.

37
00:02:28,234 --> 00:02:33,912
Calendly emails the confirmation, and the booking is noted on her client record.

38
00:02:34,412 --> 00:02:40,160
Lexington adds a first-available option, and other centers show a simple list.

39
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:44,541
If the record note can’t be saved, the booking still stands, and the client gets a

40
00:02:44,591 --> 00:02:46,519
retry button.

41
00:02:47,419 --> 00:02:50,413
So behind the scenes, there are five handoffs.

42
00:02:50,463 --> 00:02:54,372
The ZIP picks the center. Continue saves the contact.

43
00:02:54,422 --> 00:02:58,122
Register records the client. The coach’s calendar opens.

44
00:02:58,172 --> 00:03:00,762
And the booking lands on the record.

45
00:03:01,762 --> 00:03:06,217
Registering a client yourself? Start a new registration clears the form for the next

46
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:07,835
person.

47
00:03:07,935 --> 00:03:16,887
Clients who get stuck can call 1-888-414-7232, weekdays from 8 to 5.

48
00:03:17,787 --> 00:03:23,163
Coach Connect. Register, match, and book, all in one visit.

49
00:03:23,263 --> 00:03:28,221
Send clients to register.kentuckysbdc.com.
